all right so yesterday was day one of  the democratic national convention  i did a live stream of the entire thing  i was commenting i was reading viewer  comments as it was all going on  and um i i don't know  how else to start other than to say it  really wasn't very good now i'll talk  about what expectations  are and how it compares to expectations  and to what  we would expect from trump and i'm going  to contextualize it but there's no way  that i could  come to you today and say i'm so inspire  inspired and invigorated and energized  by what we saw  yesterday um i sent some  early tweets like during the first half  hour  which were really quite negative i said  first off quote  i could have done without the prayer to  jesus to kick off the dnc  not sure about anybody else and i get  that everybody does it and joe biden's  catholic and there's still a pretense  about  religion in the democratic party and  it's not just necessarily a pretense  there are religious people as well and  that that's fine  um they do the pledge of allegiance like  it all just smelled  at this point like republican light  which maybe is the goal and arguably is  still a big part of the  the centrist elements of the democratic  party so i'm not acting surprised by  that i'm just saying  it didn't really resonate with me then  sort of about 20  22 minutes in in fact i said someone  please talk me off the ledge i want to  win and the first 22 minutes of this dnc  i'm scared can someone tell me how great  this is or something  but you know then it did start to  improve and maybe my view was skewed by  the fact that i just hate cliche  packaged politics and that's exactly  what the dnc  the democratic national convention is  designed to be it's designed  to be a package culminating with the  nomination  of in this case joe biden in 2016 26  2012 different people  to get to the election and it's a  package and especially  when you've got coronavirus so it's not  just  the idea of packaging up a candidate and  a platform  but it is quite literally a video  package that has been pre-produced  in combination with live segments you  have no crowd  energy it might be just as bad with the  republican national convention and this  may be just what it is  but it felt very low energy and you know  they'd have an actual  okay speech and then they'd cut  to music or some other kind of interlude  that didn't make sense and took energy  away  but i want to try to really see this as  not  my reaction you know maybe this is the  right thing  like they don't need to convince me i'm  already voting for joe biden  and i actually don't even understand  being undecided at this point  and so maybe this is about a very sort  of  polished inoffensive package  meant to appeal to the few people that  might actually be unsure about who to  vote for like  i don't know is the point but given the  opportunity for democrats to do  something  knowing republicans will also have an  opportunity to do the same thing next  week  i'd rather have the better convention  than the worst one no matter how much it  really matters  in the end now it did keep improving  during the first two hours during the  two hours of the first day  i thought the best parts of the evening  were a woman named  kristen urkisa whose father died of  coronavirus  after voting for donald trump she spoke  really well  and authentically and a lot of the stuff  felt inauthentic  she was really good and then from the  big names  listen bernie was excellent bernie is  always just so clear and precise  with his message and the stakes and i  like that bernie  spoke specifically to his supporters  from both 2016 and 2020 and talked about  the importance  of voting for joe biden this time around  because of the existential threat that  is donald trump let's look at like a  minute of that  my friends i say to you to everyone who  supported  other candidates in the primary and to  those who may have voted for donald  trump  